{"uid":"999fb3ae71359334","name":"test_commit_import_handler_category_column_sqli_no_longer_reaches_transaction","fullName":"tests.unit.test_import_command_handlers#test_commit_import_handler_category_column_sqli_no_longer_reaches_transaction","historyId":"1803e47d7dd9080421518d5930eed985","time":{"start":1789824838381,"stop":1789824838382,"duration":1},"description":"FINTRACK-17 behaviour change (ADR-012, decision D): the CSV's own\n    category/type column is no longer used as transaction category data\n    at all -- apply_auto_categorisation() always assigns either a rule\n    match or \"Uncategorised\" during staging, regardless of what that\n    column held. So SQLi-shaped content placed in the category column\n    (as FINTRACK-16's equivalent test exercised) never reaches\n    Transaction.new() as a category value in the first place, and the\n    row commits cleanly. This is a stronger guarantee than \"rejected and\n    skipped at commit\" -- the vector is closed structurally, not just\n    caught defensively. See\n    test_commit_import_handler_skips_a_row_whose_note_is_sqli_shaped\n    below for the vector that's still live (the description/note\n    column, which does still flow into Transaction.new()).","descriptionHtml":"<p>FINTRACK-17 behaviour change (ADR-012, decision D): the CSV's own<br />\ncategory/type column is no longer used as transaction category data<br />\nat all -- apply_auto_categorisation() always assigns either a rule<br />\nmatch or &quot;Uncategorised&quot; during staging, regardless of what that<br />\ncolumn held. So SQLi-shaped content placed in the category column<br />\n(as FINTRACK-16's equivalent test exercised) never reaches<br />\nTransaction.new() as a category value in the first place, and the<br />\nrow commits cleanly. This is a stronger guarantee than &quot;rejected and<br />\nskipped at commit&quot; -- the vector is closed structurally, not just<br />\ncaught defensively. See<br />\ntest_commit_import_handler_skips_a_row_whose_note_is_sqli_shaped<br />\nbelow for the vector that's still live (the description/note<br />\ncolumn, which does still flow into Transaction.new()).</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1789824836506,"stop":1789824836506,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"caplog","time":{"start":1789824838379,"stop":1789824838379,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop","time":{"start":1789824838379,"stop":1789824838379,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_capture_fintrack_logs","time":{"start":1789824838379,"stop":1789824838379,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_flush_redis","time":{"start":1789824838380,"stop":1789824838380,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_reset_rate_limiter","time":{"start":1789824838380,"stop":1789824838380,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"transactions","time":{"start":1789824838380,"stop":1789824838380,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachment